openSW — reading SolidWorks part files without SolidWorks

This project's understanding of the .SLDPRT container draws on publicly
published reverse-engineering work by others. Facts about a file format are
not protectable; the code expressing them is. Where an implementation was
informed by a third-party project, that project is credited here.

  cadmpeg (https://github.com/cadmpeg/cadmpeg)
      Code under Apache-2.0, format documentation under CC-BY-4.0.
      Source of the block-container frame, the cache-cell and tail-directory
      shapes, the nibble-swapped section names, the __ZLB / section wrapper
      layout, and the Parasolid stream header.

  openswx (https://github.com/schwitters/openswx)
      MIT. Original description of the modern block container and its marker.

  blussyya/sldprt-format-research (https://github.com/blussyya/sldprt-format-research)
      MIT. Methodology, and the negative result that Contents/DisplayLists is
      the display tessellation rather than the B-rep.

  CosmicFrontierLabs/solid-diff (https://github.com/CosmicFrontierLabs/solid-diff)
      No licence stated — consulted as documentation only. No code copied.

  Oblikovati (https://github.com/Oblikovati/Oblikovati)
      GPL-2.0 — consulted as documentation only. No code copied.

